# This repo is developed on Windows (core.autocrlf=true) and deployed to Ubuntu. Anything that a
# Linux shell or systemd has to parse must keep LF endings — a CRLF shell script fails on Linux with
# a "bad interpreter: /usr/bin/env bash^M" error that names the shebang line rather than the real
# cause, and a systemd unit with CRLF silently mis-parses its values.
*.sh        text eol=lf
*.service   text eol=lf

# The server-side environment file template is read by systemd's EnvironmentFile parser, which
# treats a trailing CR as part of the value — a connection string would arrive subtly wrong.
*.env       text eol=lf
*.env.example text eol=lf
